WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.710
Friday night. A small café
kitchen is swamped with orders.

2
00:00:04.710 --> 00:00:07.370
One cook makes 10 meals an hour.

3
00:00:07.370 --> 00:00:10.270
Hire a second, and the kitchen makes 24.

4
00:00:10.270 --> 00:00:11.830
That's more than double!

5
00:00:11.830 --> 00:00:14.030
So the owner keeps hiring.

6
00:00:14.030 --> 00:00:15.670
Three cooks. Four.

7
00:00:15.670 --> 00:00:19.470
Five. If a kitchen hires
twice as many cooks,

8
00:00:19.470 --> 00:00:22.430
why might it not make twice as many meals?

9
00:00:22.430 --> 00:00:25.090
In this mission, you'll
measure what each new cook

10
00:00:25.090 --> 00:00:27.560
really adds to the kitchen's output.

11
00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:30.430
Then you'll add cooks
one by one and predict

12
00:00:30.430 --> 00:00:32.500
what happens to the meal count.

13
00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:35.570
Your mission: find out
why more hands do not

14
00:00:35.570 --> 00:00:38.350
always mean proportionally more output.
